WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.394
Hi! What does a tadpole grow into? Where does a chick come from? Today we'll look at the frog and chicken life cycles, and compare them.

2
00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:14.826
A frog lays eggs in water, in clumps.

3
00:00:14.976 --> 00:00:21.066
Tadpoles hatch from the eggs. They live in water, have a tail and breathe with gills.

4
00:00:21.216 --> 00:00:27.594
The tadpole grows back legs and front legs, its tail gets shorter, and it becomes a froglet.

5
00:00:27.744 --> 00:00:34.554
The adult frog has no tail, breathes with lungs, and lives in water and on land.

6
00:00:34.704 --> 00:00:39.762
A chicken's life cycle has three stages: egg, chick and adult.

7
00:00:39.912 --> 00:00:45.786
The hen sits on the eggs to keep them warm. After about three weeks, chicks hatch.

8
00:00:45.936 --> 00:00:50.298
A chick looks like the adult, only smaller and fluffy.

9
00:00:50.448 --> 00:01:00.714
Compare: the frog has four stages and the chicken three. Do the young look like the adults? Tadpoles don't, but chicks do.

10
00:01:00.864 --> 00:01:07.434
Watch out! Some pupils think tadpoles breathe with lungs like frogs. That's wrong!

11
00:01:07.584 --> 00:01:13.818
Tadpoles live in water and breathe with gills. Only adult frogs breathe with lungs.

12
00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:19.938
During its life, a frog changes both its shape and how it breathes.

13
00:01:20.088 --> 00:01:28.554
Your turn! A tadpole is the young of which animal? Pause and think.

14
00:01:28.704 --> 00:01:34.266
A tadpole grows into a frog. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:34.416 --> 00:01:42.570
Another one! What does a tadpole breathe with? Pause and think.

16
00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:48.114
A tadpole breathes with gills. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:48.264 --> 00:01:57.330
Here's another! How many stages are in a chicken's life cycle? Pause and think.

18
00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:03.114
Three: egg, chick and adult. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:03.264 --> 00:02:13.122
Try one more! How does a tadpole's body change as it becomes a froglet? Pause and think.

20
00:02:13.272 --> 00:02:19.146
It grows legs and its tail gets shorter. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:19.296 --> 00:02:29.250
Try one more! Whose young look like the adult, the chicken's or the frog's? Pause and think.

22
00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:36.738
Chicks look like adult chickens, but tadpoles don't look like frogs. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:36.888 --> 00:02:45.042
Last one! What does an adult frog breathe with? Pause and think.

24
00:02:45.192 --> 00:02:52.194
An adult frog breathes with lungs, so it can live on land too. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:52.344 --> 00:03:05.058
Remember: frogs have four stages, with tadpoles using gills and adults lungs. Chickens have three stages, and chicks look like adults. Different animals have different numbers of stages.

26
00:03:05.208 --> 00:03:10.578
Draw a frog's life cycle and explain it to your family!

